1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
You built an app.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:06,500
Somebody, someday, will ask what it's worth.

3
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:11,000
Most calculators hand you a number.

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:15,000
And keep the reasoning to themselves.
So here is the reasoning.

5
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,700
Your revenue is a surface.

6
00:00:18,700 --> 00:00:22,000
Price on one side, customers on the other.

7
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:24,700
Double either one, and you double the area.

8
00:00:24,700 --> 00:00:27,000
But only one of them is free.

9
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:30,000
So where does that put you?

10
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,300
On the pricing ladder, Spotify is a mouse:
€2 a month per user.

11
00:00:33,300 --> 00:00:35,700
Shopify is a deer, at €75.

12
00:00:35,700 --> 00:00:38,000
Salesforce is a whale.

13
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Your price per customer decides your trade.

14
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:45,000
But growing is not enough.

15
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:48,300
Direct costs, acquisition, fixed costs.

16
00:00:48,300 --> 00:00:50,700
Each one takes its share.

17
00:00:50,700 --> 00:00:53,000
No profit, no multiple.

18
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:56,700
Then nine lines build that multiple.

19
00:00:56,700 --> 00:00:59,700
Churn. Growth. Retention. Client concentration.

20
00:00:59,700 --> 00:01:02,000
And how much of the company walks out
of the door with you.

21
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:05,000
Every one of them, named.

22
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Colombes. Free. No sign-up.
